          "explanation": "In The Radicalism of the American Revolution (1992), Gordon Wood argued that the Revolution transformed American society, sweeping away a world of kings, aristocrats, and deference and opening the way to democracy. Zinn stresses continuity: an elite that kept power and a promise of equality that excluded most people. Their disagreement is about how much really changed, and for whom.",
