          "explanation": "Zinn grants that the Revolution was real -- hence \"a kind of revolution,\" not \"no revolution.\" His claim is that elites needed the energy of poor soldiers, farmers, and artisans, but the political and economic order that followed protected men of property. The tempting wrong answer, \"a fraud that changed nothing,\" overstates him: he acknowledges real gains for some groups while arguing the gains were unevenly shared.",
