          "explanation": "Zinn stresses that Polk sent troops into territory both nations claimed, then presented the resulting clash as an attack on American soil. He foregrounds the dissent of Whigs like Lincoln, abolitionists, Thoreau, and the thousands of soldiers who deserted. The first option is the war's official justification in 1846, which Zinn rejects. The last is contradicted by the roughly 9,000 desertions he highlights.",
