          "explanation": "Zinn argues that leaders and business voices of the 1890s spoke openly about surplus goods needing foreign markets, and that the depression of 1893 and waves of strikes made this urgent. He also suggests a patriotic war offered unity across class lines. He doesn't deny that many Americans sincerely sympathized with Cubans -- he argues that sympathy was not what drove policy.",
