          "explanation": "Zinn condemns the September 11 attacks as terrorism and a crime. His objection is to the response: he argues that bombing Afghanistan killed civilians as innocent as the attacks' victims, that war produces fresh anger and more terrorism, and that the PATRIOT Act threatened civil liberties. He urges asking why the attackers hated the United States -- pointing to U.S. foreign policy -- and pursuing terrorists as criminals rather than waging open-ended war.",
